  "description": "Illustrates the value for a star's mass.",
  "definition": "Measured in solar masses ($M_{\\odot}$), where 1 is the mass of our Sun. Most known host stars range from low-mass red dwarfs (~0.1 $M_{\\odot}$) to stars several times more massive than the Sun."
